ooks having said that if she  likes a sipper and it feels good to her  and it doesn't seem to like erode her  teeth or upset her stomach as it does  for a lot of us then hey like i say sip  sip away you go girl for this recipe i'm  using three eggs which will amount to  about 18 grams worth of protein i try  and aim to have about 25 grams of  protein per each meal just for my own  goals so just having three eggs is a  little bit low for my protein needs so  for this recipe instead of the avocado  i'm going to be swapping that out for a  little bit of a high quality grass-fed  cheese so instead i can get the fat but  also a little bit of protein to add onto  the eggs with the cheese and then for a  fiber component i'm using about a cup of  spinach meal will typically be around 2  30 p.m again this looks delicious and i  love that we've got a solid amount of  fiber protein and fat but again where  are the carbs intermittent fasting is  restrictive enough for most people so we  also layer in low carb like most people  would find it really hard to feel  emotionally satisfied like folks let's  not burn the candle at both ends i don't  snack between meals this is so crucial  to make sure that you're still getting  the gut healing benefits and if you're  having difficulties losing weight  getting more of those breaks between  meals can help the body to more easily  shift back into fat burning yes and  probably not yes for folks who have  compromised guts like those of us with a  history of sibo for whom stimulating  that migratory motor complex is really  super key we do want to try to give our  bodies a solid few hours between meals  most healthy guts don't have to be so  deliberate about it since the mmc only  takes about an hour and a half to two  hours to complete but yes if she has a  history of functional gut disorders  trying to space out meals and snacks  does have merit as for fat burning  theoretically yes but in practice not a  big deal as i discussed in my video on  intermittent fasting and insulin here  insulin is a fat storage hormone on  paper but in real life it doesn't seem  to have a huge impact on weight gain or  loss when at energy balance it doesn't  like cheat the dieting system so to  speak and we know this because when the  calorie deficit is the same folks with  and without diabetes or insulin  resistance will lose about the same  amount of weight so while a higher carb  or like a grazing diet does transiently  increase insulin levels which kind of  boots you out of that fat burning mode  it doesn't seem to affect weight without  like a caloric surplus or deficit we're  kind of splitting hairs here again let's  think big picture so my last meal of the  day for tonight is going to be my  pumpkin chili it's extremely simple and  also the protein component is really  versatile this looks delicious but  surprise surprise still keeping it  low-carb over here  i mean i'm shocked and if this like  lights up her life great i just know  that even if i ate like a huge bowl of  that chili i would not be able to go to  bed feeling satisfied i would absolutely  find myself craving carbs in the several  hours from 7 30 p.m to whenever she goes  to bed and like immediately upon waking  and that's why i don't love intermittent  fasting for a lot of people in fact we  can talk about the insulin suppressing  and the growth hormone stimulating  benefits all we want but as i discussed  in my intermittent fasting video right  here the effects that these factors have  on a healthy body are actually really  small evidence suggests that small  natural variations in human growth  hormone have little to no effect on  weight loss and insulin levels are  tightly regulated in healthy people so  they don't really have a huge impact on  weight loss either and most of the  insulin benefits in fasting occurs when  you front load your carbs in the morning  and then cut off eating by midday but  autumn like most fasters aren't doing  early time restricted eating so she's  not actually really getting the benefits  that she obsesses over in every video  and yet these two things are often  touted as the secret to why intermittent  fasting is different when in reality if  we just eat fewer meals we tend to  actually eat less we're just kind of bad  at making up for missed calories that my  friends is ultimately what results in  weight loss i mean as far as i'm  concerned autumn worked out like three  times in the day and ate under 1700  calories only 27 of which were carbs i  would also lose weight or maintain a  very lean body composition if i kept my  glycogen stores depleted and was in a  chronic caloric deficit like that i  gotta say like i bought autumn's ebook  and while i appreciate that there were  34 studies cited which is a lot more  than most wellness influencers would  cite she seems to overlook a lot of key  studies that would refute or downplay  her position and ultimately i feel like  a lot of it is missing the forest from  the trees for most people intermittent  fasting isn't the holy grail to health  it's a tool in the toolbox that works  for some people because we suck at  making up for the calories when we skip  a meal in some people it actually  results in weight gain and in extreme  cases it may be dangerous for hormones  so it's not benign and it's not  appropriate for a lot of people i think  ultimately if you feel good eating on a  particular regimented schedule then  whatever like it makes sense for you to  continue to eat that way autumn should  feel empowered to eat low carb and to  fast because it seems to work for her  but when an influencer recommends a  singular way of eating to others and  monetizes a how-to program on it to the  public then i just expect them to be  transparent and based on everything i've  shared i'm not convinced by the  one-sided data consistently cited and  shared now to throw autumn a bone i will  say that i think autumn does offer a ton  of great recommendations and tips for  newbie and advanced intermittent fasters  so if this is a way of eating that works  for you and you enjoy definitely check  that out but i do think the low carb  recipes and the fasting regimen would be  a bit of a hard pill for most to swallow  but on that note that is all that i have  for you guys today thanks again to  buildbar for sponsoring if you like this  video be sure to give it the thumbs up  leave me a comment below on who you'd  like to see me review next subscribe to  the channel and i'll see you next time  on abby's kitchen bye  [Music]
 

